  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $\\frac{b+c}{11}=\\frac{c+a}{12}=\\frac{a+b}{13}=K$ in a triangle $A B C$. $\\Rightarrow b+c=11 K, c+a=12 K, a+b=13 K$ On solving these, we get $a=7 K, b=6 K, c=5 K$\nNow we know,\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\cos A=\\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2 b c} \\\\\n& =\\frac{36 K^2+25 K^2-49 K^2}{2(6 K) 5 K}=\\frac{1}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
